2026-06-05 17:20:13.263 | DEBUG  | logging:callHandlers:1737 | Submitting callback functools.partial(<built-in method run of _contextvars.Context object at 0x1650df480>, <bound method Embedder._embed_sync of <src.embedder.Embedder object at 0x1320a3b60>>, "[SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE TRAINING CURRICULUM- Zamora.docx - CROSS-CUTTING THEMES]\nThe LEAD Project integrates several key themes to ensure a holistic and sustainable impact on the lives of participants and their communities.\nNutrition and Health: The project goes beyond simply growing food by actively promoting dietary diversity. Participants learn about the importance of a balanced diet that includes a variety of vegetables and cereals, as well as essential practices in food safety, hygiene, and sanitation.\nGender and Youth Inclusion: The project is committed to inclusivity, with a specific goal of ensuring at least 50% of participants are women. It also actively encourages youth to take on leadership roles, ensuring their voices and skills are central to the project's success.\nEnvironmental Sustainability: Sustainable practices are at the core of the agricultural training. The curriculum includes vital techniques for soil and water conservation, such as mulching, creating Zai pits, and integrating agroforestry to protect natural resources and build long-term resilience.\nProtection and Safeguarding: The project prioritizes the safety and well-being of all participants. All training spaces are designed to be safe and respectful, and the project strictly adheres to the Do No Harm and Protection from Sexual Exploitation and Abuse (PSEA) principles.\nMarket Linkages and Entrepreneurship: To support economic empowerment, the project strengthens farm-to-market approaches. Participants are equipped with the basic agribusiness skills needed to turn their farming activities into profitable enterprises, ensuring they can effectively sell their produce and thrive in the local market.", False) with args () and kwargs {} to thread worker queue
