2026-06-05 17:20:20.211 | DEBUG  | logging:callHandlers:1737 | Submitting callback functools.partial(<built-in method run of _contextvars.Context object at 0x1650df480>, <bound method Embedder._embed_sync of <src.embedder.Embedder object at 0x1320a3b60>>, '[SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE TRAINING CURRICULUM- Zamora.docx - EXPECTED OUTCOMES OF THE SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE TRAINING]\nUpon completing the training, participants will be equipped with a comprehensive set of skills to practice sustainable and profitable agriculture. They are expected to demonstrate the ability to:\nPlan and Prepare Land: Use climate-smart agriculture (CSA) principles to prepare land and strategically plan mixed cropping systems.\nManage Seeds and Crops: Select and handle quality seeds for a variety of crops, including cereals, vegetables, and cassava, to ensure healthy planting.\nImprove Soil Health: Effectively apply organic and other appropriate methods for managing soil fertility.\nControl Pests and Diseases: Monitor crops and implement Integrated Pest Management (IPM) techniques to control pests and diseases.\nHandle Harvests Effectively: Harvest, process, and store crops properly to minimize post-harvest losses and maximize yield.\nEngage in Financial Management: Practice financial literacy and actively participate in VSLA savings and collective marketing efforts.\nEstablish Household Gardens: Successfully replicate the skills and practices learned in the demonstration gardens on their own household plots, ensuring a continuous food supply and sustainable production.', False) with args () and kwargs {} to thread worker queue
2026-06-05 17:20:20.214 | DEBUG  | logging:callHandlers:1737 | #3 got callback functools.partial(<built-in method run of _contextvars.Context object at 0x1650df480>, <bound method Embedder._embed_sync of <src.embedder.Embedder object at 0x1320a3b60>>, '[SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE TRAINING CURRICULUM- Zamora.docx - EXPECTED OUTCOMES OF THE SUSTAINABLE AGRICULTURE TRAINING]\nUpon completing the training, participants will be equipped with a comprehensive set of skills to practice sustainable and profitable agriculture. They are expected to demonstrate the ability to:\nPlan and Prepare Land: Use climate-smart agriculture (CSA) principles to prepare land and strategically plan mixed cropping systems.\nManage Seeds and Crops: Select and handle quality seeds for a variety of crops, including cereals, vegetables, and cassava, to ensure healthy planting.\nImprove Soil Health: Effectively apply organic and other appropriate methods for managing soil fertility.\nControl Pests and Diseases: Monitor crops and implement Integrated Pest Management (IPM) techniques to control pests and diseases.\nHandle Harvests Effectively: Harvest, process, and store crops properly to minimize post-harvest losses and maximize yield.\nEngage in Financial Management: Practice financial literacy and actively participate in VSLA savings and collective marketing efforts.\nEstablish Household Gardens: Successfully replicate the skills and practices learned in the demonstration gardens on their own household plots, ensuring a continuous food supply and sustainable production.', False) with args () and kwargs {} from queue
